   Supplied by their industry and scavenged technologies, there is no shortage of surplus weaponry for the [color=tan]Dynasty[/color] to throw their weight around with. Due to their very recently-established RND program, they are initially quite set back technologically compared to the TSF. However,
   their close proximity to the Colossus Radius has allowed them untold access to the riches within the system, and their hardened military-industrial complex has been quick to adapt with their newly acquired unobtainium.

  [color=green]Strengths:[/color]
  - Having a semi-dated arsenal means there is no direct counter like EMP to combat styles among the [color=tan]Vanguard[/color]. You either overpower or out-skill them in firepower.
  - While many of their weapons are built around rare materials from the Colossus Radius, many patterns are relatively cheap to construct.

  [color=red]Weaknesses:[/color]
  - Weaponry is only supplied through merit. Soldiers need to prove themselves by gathering anomalous findings or stealing enemy equipment to gain the materials necessary for better gear.
  - While the PDV have many brute-force options reminiscent of their past on Pizk, including advanced armor and weapons, they do not have the same level of mastery over normal materials like the TSF do.

